## Execution Steps

### 1. Access Application Server 3
From the jump host, log into Application Server 3 using the credentials provided:
```bash
ssh banner@stapp03
2. Access the Docker Container
Locate and access the running kkloud container interactively:

Bash
sudo docker ps
sudo docker exec -it kkloud bash
3. Install Apache2
Update the package lists and install Apache inside the container:

Bash
apt-get update
apt-get install -y apache2
4. Configure Apache to Listen on Port 3003
Update the global ports configuration file to listen on port 3003 without restricting it to a specific IP address:

Bash
sed -i 's/Listen 80/Listen 3003/g' /etc/apache2/ports.conf
Update the default virtual host configuration block to match the new port:

Bash
sed -i 's/<VirtualHost \*:80>/<VirtualHost \*:3003>/g' /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf
5. Start Apache Service
Start the Apache web server inside the container and keep the container running:

Bash
service apache2 start
